xgameruntime: the add-ons the player owns, their licences, and the gamer picture (MetalHorizon 1.1.1, issue #18)

Forza Horizon 6 priced add-ons the player had bought, saw no VIP membership, and showed a grey profile picture:
nothing was ever owned here, and the picture was a neutral square. With MetalHorizon's xodus-service 1.1.1:
- Store catalog protocol 2 (CSDX): the request carries flags (1: what the account owns, only) and the answer the
  products of it the account owns, from the Store's collections resolved against the catalog (editions and bundles
  count with what they contain). Those products and their SKUs come back in the user's collection (quantity 1).
- XStoreQueryEntitledProductsAsync asks for the game and the add-ons the account owns; XStoreQueryAddOnLicensesAsync
  answers their licences ("<Store ID>/<SKU>", the developer's offer token, active, no end).
- XUserGetGamerPictureAsync asks the service for the account's own picture (GSDX frames: the profile's
  GameDisplayPicRaw, as a PNG of the size asked), on a thread of ours.
Whenever the service cannot answer (none, an older one, Microsoft unreachable), the game gets what it got before:
the game alone among the entitled products, no add-on licence, the grey picture, and never an error.
Tested without the game: engine/tests/store-ownership.

